# Voxtype owns its own config.toml. Observed at the 2026-10-24 daemon start:
# it serialised the whole file, reordered the comments and left a .bak beside
# it. A stow symlink would write that serialisation straight into this public
# repository. The tracked file is the seed instead; bootstrap copies it only
# where the machine has none, and voxtype owns it from then on.
#
# A custom list replaces stow's defaults, so the list's own file is ignored too.
\.stow-local-ignore
config\.toml
